    id: 'Why-Small-Businesses-Are-Carrying-America-on-Their-Backs',
    title: 'Why Small Businesses Are Carrying America on Their Backs',
    content: 'Small businesses rarely make headlines, yet they quietly sustain the American economy. They create jobs, stabilize communities, and take risks larger institutions avoid.\n\nThese businesses operate without massive buffers. When conditions change, owners adapt quickly or absorb the consequences personally. Success is earned through persistence rather than scale.\n\nBeyond economics, small businesses shape culture. They sponsor local events, support schools, and create gathering places that anchor towns.\n\nAs consolidation increases across industries, the role of small business becomes even more critical. They preserve competition, encourage innovation, and keep economic power distributed.\n\nSmall businesses do not ask for recognition. They simply keep going.',
